WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
(computerized music)

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.909
- [Narrator] Tetris.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:06.626
It transcends age, culture, and language.

00:00:06.626 --> 00:00:09.096
It's a gamer and non-gamer's game.

00:00:09.096 --> 00:00:12.425
But did you know Tetris has a Soviet past?

00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:16.279
(computerized music)

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:20.096
Tetris is the brainchild of
this man, Alexey Pajitnov.

00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:22.650
Alexey was a computer
programmer in Russia.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.149
He worked for the Soviet Union,

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:26.495
at the Moscow Academy of Sciences.

00:00:26.495 --> 00:00:28.806
Alexey always had a propensity for math,

00:00:28.806 --> 00:00:30.506
computers, and puzzles.

00:00:30.506 --> 00:00:32.212
It was that propensity that led him

00:00:32.212 --> 00:00:36.220
to the creation of the best
video game of all time.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.667
He drew inspiration from a
little known game, Pentominoes.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.454
Pentominoes was a puzzle board game

00:00:41.454 --> 00:00:44.212
in which you had to fit
geometric shapes together.

00:00:44.212 --> 00:00:46.526
Alexey took the principles
from Pentominoes,

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:48.875
upgraded them, and
created a computer game.

00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:50.820
Originally only intended for himself,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.499
he named the game Tetris for two reasons.

00:00:53.499 --> 00:00:56.539
It's a combination of tetra,
the Greek word meaning four,

00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:59.739
and tennis, Pajitnov's favorite sport.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:02.094
Because Tetris was
created during work hours,

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.923
the Soviet Union claimed all rights

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:06.756
to both Tetris, and all royalties.

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:09.541
Fast forward to 1996,

00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:13.278
the rights to Tetris were
finally signed over to Pajitnov.

00:01:13.278 --> 00:01:15.061
Tetris taps into our universal need

00:01:15.061 --> 00:01:16.642
to create order out of chaos,

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.141
which is ultimately why it's one

00:01:18.141 --> 00:01:20.312
of the most iconic games in history.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.895
(Upbeat music)

